# IMPORTANT — no `200` rewrite rules here on purpose.
# Cloudflare Pages does NOT support 200 rewrites in _redirects (that is a
# Netlify feature); it treats them as redirects, which CHANGES the URL and
# strips the locale prefix (/at/produkt/x → /Produkt). All locale routing is
# therefore done as a real rewrite in functions/[[path]].js, which serves the
# underlying HTML while keeping the visible URL intact.
#
# Locale routes handled in functions/[[path]].js:
#   /{locale}/                 → index.html
#   /{locale}/produkt/<handle> → Produkt.html
#   /{locale}/<page>.html      → <page>.html
#   /produkt/<handle>          → Produkt.html   (no-prefix fallback)

# Retired legacy per-chapter pages → new product template (keeps old links alive)
/Der%20Fluesterwald%20v3.html            /produkt/kapitel-1-fluesterwald  301
/Der%20Silbersee%20-%20Kapitel%202.html  /produkt/kapitel-2-silbersee     301
/Der Fluesterwald v3.html                /produkt/kapitel-1-fluesterwald  301
/Der Silbersee - Kapitel 2.html          /produkt/kapitel-2-silbersee     301
